\c 10
\s1 Samuel Anoints Saul
\p \v 1 \w Then Samuel|strong="H8050"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w a flask|strong="H6378"\w* \w of oil|strong="H8081"\w*, \w poured it|strong="H3332"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w Saul’s head|strong="H7218"\w*, \w kissed him|strong="H5401"\w*, \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Has not|strong="H3808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H3588"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w anointed you|strong="H4886"\w* \w ruler|strong="H5057"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w His inheritance|strong="H5159"\w*?\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa “Has not the LORD anointed you ruler over Israel? And you will rule over the LORD’s people and save them from their enemies around them. This will be the sign to you that the LORD has appointed you to be leader over His inheritance.\f* \v 2 \w When you leave|strong="H1980"\w* \w me|strong="H5978"\w* \w today|strong="H3117"\w*, \w you will find|strong="H4672"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w at|strong="H5973"\w* \w Rachel’s|strong="H7354"\w* \w tomb|strong="H6900"\w* \w in Zelzah|strong="H6766"\w* \w on the border|strong="H1366"\w* \w of Benjamin|strong="H1144"\w*. \w They will say|strong="H559"\w* \w to you|strong="H413"\w*, ‘\w The donkeys|strong="H860"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w you seek|strong="H1980"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1245"\w* \w have been found|strong="H4672"\w*, \w and now|strong="H2009"\w* \w your father|strong="H1"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w has stopped|strong="H5203"\w* \w worrying about|strong="H1697"\w* \w the donkeys|strong="H860"\w* \w and started worrying|strong="H1672"\w* about you, \w asking|strong="H559"\w*, “\w What|strong="H4100"\w* \w should I do|strong="H6213"\w* \w about my son|strong="H1121"\w*?”’
